                <item name="Name" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Panel</item>
              </items>
              <chunks count="1">
                <chunk name="Container">
                  <items count="9">
                    <item name="Description" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">A panel for custom notes and text values</item>
                    <item name="InstanceGuid" type_name="gh_guid" type_code="9">b52aaab8-d53d-4752-ac84-25559b9dd5a0</item>
                    <item name="Locked" type_name="gh_bool" type_code="1">true</item>
                    <item name="Name" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Panel</item>
                    <item name="NickName" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">SIX-EIGHT CROSS BOND</item>
                    <item name="Optional" type_name="gh_bool" type_code="1">false</item>
                    <item name="ScrollRatio" type_name="gh_double" type_code="6">0</item>
                    <item name="SourceCount" type_name="gh_int32" type_code="3">0</item>
                    <item name="UserText" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">SIX-EIGHT CROSS BOND / 19 LAYERS
Odd banks: 6 bricks = 2 x 3. Even banks: 8 bricks = 4 x 2.
odd_to_even 2 mm / even_to_odd 8 mm, so the fragile transition advances less.
rot_step is ONE cumulative increment, default 3.5 degrees. heading_deg rotates the complete bridge.
The bank path follows the previous course axis; height, opening and top-view path are a compromise from the old 13-layer form.
Crown closure uses 6 bricks in 3 x 2, including bricks connecting BOTH banks.
Local bearing is distinct from whole-stack equilibrium. Robot frames are generated automatically. Structural analysis does not gate frame output. Sender stays locked.
ROBOT FRAME ADAPTER: connect Data 1 OR Data 2 directly. No CHECK button is needed.
This conversion is not a structural or collision approval. TCP, dispenser, program and shape settings are preserved from the source file.</item>
                  </items>
